# Project Tech Stack
- PHP Version: 8.2
- Framework: Laravel 11.x (Vite build system)
- Node.js Version: 24.x
- Frontend: Vue 3 (Composition API / <script setup>), A-Frame (WebVR/AR)

# Output & Response Constraints
- Always provide explanations, comments, and interactive responses in Japanese.
- Skip verbose internal reasoning or thinking text to save tokens; output direct implementation code.
- Do not add unrequested features. Focus strictly on the specific task assigned.
- Keep code changes minimal, concise, and elegant.
- Ask clarifying questions whenever requirements or instructions are ambiguous.

# Coding Standards & Guidelines
- Follow active PSR standards (PSR-1, PSR-2, PSR-12) for all PHP/Laravel code.
- Adhere strictly to Laravel 11 structure (routes in routes/web.php, config in config/ or .env).
- Write Vue 3 components using <script setup> and Composition API.
- Safely integrate A-Frame logic within Vue lifecycle hooks (onMounted / onUnmounted).
- Prioritize predictability over cleverness.
- Handle edge cases explicitly (empty states, missing files, permission errors).

# Safety & Execution Rules
- Execution Shell: The terminal shell is MSYS (Git Bash) on Windows. Use POSIX/Bash compatible commands and syntax.
- Target ONLY files within the current relative directory (./). NEVER use absolute paths or search parent directories.
- ALWAYS run `php -l [PHP_FILE_NAME]` to verify syntax before finishing any PHP code task.
- ALWAYS test and verify code changes—do not assume code works without checking.
- Preserve existing correct functionality unless explicitly instructed to change it.
- Resolve errors immediately at the current step. Never ignore errors or proceed to the next step prematurely.

# AR Stamp Rally Cross-Platform Rules
- For ARstampRally development, ensure error-free execution on both platforms:
  - Android: Chrome native WebXR API.
  - iOS: Safari (WebXR unsupported) via AR.js / Three.js custom implementations, or fallback to USDZ Quick Look.

# Task & Workflow Management
- Requirements & Design First: Never implement without proper specification. When adding a new web app or feature, document first in `requirements.md`, `design.md`, and `tasks.md`.
- Phase Start Declaration: Report "前段階のmdファイルを読み込みました" before starting work on a new phase.
- File Handling: Inspect current file contents before editing. When recreating files, clear obsolete content and write clean code from scratch.
- Step-by-Step Execution: Implement incrementally with small changes. Do not run multiple tasks in parallel. Validate expected outcomes at each step.
- Documentation Update: Update code comments and `README.md` upon completion of implementation.